cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite both the software (this file) and the underlying thesis (see preferred-citation)."
title: "attention-screening: framework for protein-ligand interaction prediction on kinases"
abstract: |
  Open-source framework for kinase-ligand bioactivity prediction via attention-based
  semantic screening over linear sequences (amino acids + SMILES). Implements DT-Kinase
  (ESM-2 8M + MoLFormer + cross-attention 2D + CNN + hierarchical attention pooling)
  and a unified evaluation protocol for three published baselines (DrugBAN, GraphBAN,
  ConPLex). Provides scaffold-split universal partitioning, statistical refinements
  for paired comparison (deduplication by pair, block bootstrap by protein, consensual
  threshold rule) and a multi-model committee validated as the optimal operational
  configuration.
